From fcd65ba21d8c45204fe2f06aca7e543e588bfa00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:50:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: let the PHY go when the DP controller suspends

The display subsystem powers off with a command mode panel switched off,
and the DP controller loses its state with it. Runtime suspend
deinitialized the controller but left the PHY marked initialized, so
the next plug did not set it up again and every AUX transfer timed out:
a monitor plugged in while the phone's screen was off hung detection
for half a minute.

A DP controller only runtime suspends with nothing plugged in, so exit
the PHY on suspend for DP as for eDP; detection and the plug handler set
it up again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 28331b05c322..0c3f72185b2b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1590,10 +1590,16 @@ static int msm_dp_pm_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 
 	disable_irq(dp->irq);
 
-	if (dp->msm_dp_display.is_edp) {
-		msm_dp_display_host_phy_exit(dp);
+	/*
+	 * The controller loses its state while the display subsystem is
+	 * powered off, as with a command mode panel switched off. A PHY left
+	 * marked initialized would then not be set up again on the next
+	 * plug, and every AUX transfer would time out. A DP controller only
+	 * suspends with nothing plugged in, so let the PHY go as well.
+	 */
+	msm_dp_display_host_phy_exit(dp);
+	if (dp->msm_dp_display.is_edp)
 		msm_dp_aux_hpd_disable(dp->aux);
-	}
 	msm_dp_display_host_deinit(dp);
 
 	return 0;
